# fastly_service_logging_s3 (Resource)

Fastly service S3 logging endpoint resource. Writes directly to the specified writable service version.

This resource is part of the explicit/default first-class resource family. It
manages an Amazon S3 real-time logging endpoint on the configured service
version. It does not clone, activate, or stage service versions.

To have the provider manage the version lifecycle for you instead, use the
nested `logging_s3` block on `fastly_service_cdn_auto` or
`fastly_service_compute_auto` — see "Automatic-lifecycle usage" below.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_logging_s3" "example" {
  service_id  = fastly_service_cdn.example.id
  version     = 1
  name        = "s3-example"
  bucket_name = "my-log-bucket"

  authentication = {
    access_key = var.s3_access_key
    secret_key = var.s3_secret_key
  }
}
```

A fully configured endpoint, using `iam_role` instead of `access_key`/`secret_key`
to authenticate. `format`, `format_version`, `placement`, and
`response_condition` only affect generated VCL, so they are valid when
`service_id` refers to a CDN (VCL) service and rejected for a Compute service:

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_logging_s3" "iam_role" {
  service_id  = fastly_service_cdn.example.id
  version     = 1
  name        = "s3-iam-role"
  bucket_name = "my-log-bucket"
  domain      = "s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com"
  path        = "/logs/"
  period      = 1800

  authentication = {
    iam_role = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/my-fastly-logging-role"
  }
  processing_region      = "us"
  compression_codec      = "gzip"
  redundancy             = "standard_ia"
  server_side_encryption = "AES256"

  format             = "%h %l %u %t \"%r\" %>s %b"
  format_version     = 2
  placement          = "none"
  response_condition = fastly_service_condition.errors_only.name
}
```

Attaching to a Compute service — the VCL-only attributes must be omitted:

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_logging_s3" "compute" {
  service_id  = fastly_service_compute.example.id
  version     = 1
  name        = "s3-compute"
  bucket_name = "my-log-bucket"

  authentication = {
    access_key = var.s3_access_key
    secret_key = var.s3_secret_key
  }
}
```

## Automatic-lifecycle usage

Inside the `_auto` service resources, S3 logging is a nested block and the
provider clones, validates, and activates a new service version whenever the
block changes. The nested block takes the same arguments as this resource,
minus `service_id` and `version`, which the parent service owns.

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_cdn_auto" "example" {
  name = "my-service"

  logging_s3 {
    name        = "s3-example"
    bucket_name = "my-log-bucket"

    authentication = {
      access_key = var.s3_access_key
      secret_key = var.s3_secret_key
    }
  }
}
```

`fastly_service_compute_auto` supports the same block, without the VCL-only
arguments (`format`, `format_version`, `placement`, `response_condition`):

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_compute_auto" "example" {
  name = "my-compute-service"

  package {
    filename         = "package.tar.gz"
    source_code_hash = filesha512("package.tar.gz")
  }

  logging_s3 {
    name        = "s3-compute"
    bucket_name = "my-log-bucket"

    authentication = {
      access_key = var.s3_access_key
      secret_key = var.s3_secret_key
    }
  }
}
```

